  "_note": "RUN 2 of the series -- TX power x dwell. Resolves the confound left by the old TX-power x rotation run, whose every arm was attenuated (-12..-24 dBm) and which therefore established flatness only WITHIN the attenuated tail while attributing its large rotation effect (80/92/99% at 4/8/16s) to dwell alone. Here dwell 2/4/8s crosses TX {+9 dBm full, -24 dBm floor}, 6 conditions x 15 reps = 90 cells, 6-cell blocks cycling all conditions so diurnal drift is balanced. adv scales with dwell to hold broadcasts-per-key at 5 -- the series' standard transmit axis, identical to the dwell factorial and to run 4 -- so dwell means the same thing here as it does there. ~2.7h transmit. Second and larger purpose: every full-power run so far has sat on the delivery ceiling, where no parameter can be measured; this run establishes attenuation as a deliberate dial for getting below it, and run 4 then uses whichever arm lands off the ceiling. Ground truth: resweep.py. ANTENNA STATE: directional antenna FITTED. The directional antenna cannot be switched under program control, so it is a BETWEEN-RUN block, not an interleaved factor. Run this file and its counterpart back to back on one night, then REVERSE the order on a second night, so antenna state is crossed against time-of-night rather than confounded with it. The txdbm axis inside each run is interleaved and therefore clean on its own, and the anchor cells measure what the antenna itself is worth: the same reference condition runs in both states. ANCHOR CELLS: cells named a###_ref are the series' shared reference condition (incremental, adv 1s, 8s dwell, 20 windows, +9 dBm) -- the same cell the density matrix repeats 120 times. One opens every run and one follows every few blocks, ~10% of the run. They are not part of this matrix's design; they exist so any two nights can be compared against a condition they actually share, and so a night whose ambient density was unusual announces itself instead of silently biasing the comparison. Analyse them across runs first, then read the run's own contrast.",
